    "explanation": "Both parties and the record agree on the arithmetic. Under POL-RD-22 (v2.1 s1.4) the deviation is the platform's recorded distances: trip_record.actual_distance_km 5.2 km minus trip_record.optimal_distance_km 4.6 km = 0.60 km, against a tolerance of 1.0 km. The deviation is therefore within tolerance. The GPS trace is used only to show which route was taken and when; it is not used to re-measure distance.\n\nOn POL-RD-24 (v2.1 s1.3) the case falls in row (e): the reroute was not traffic-justified — the only traffic data for the recommended Bedok Road segment in the trip window, LTA advisory LTA-TI-260809-8709 (EV-ADVIS-05002-01), is type NONE, recording no incident, roadwork, closure or congestion — and the deviation is 1 km or less, so no refund is due. The same result follows on the other branch: even if the reroute were traffic-justified, row (c) (traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation 1 km or less) also returns no refund. The driver's counter-statement that 'Bedok Road got bus stop and traffic light very long' is a bare assertion of traffic which, under POL-RD-23, does not by itself justify a reroute — but it costs the driver nothing here, because the tolerance rows decide the case either way.\n\nThe driver did not notify the rider of the deviation: the chat log (EV-CHAT-05002) holds two messages only, both sent at 11:26 and both about the pickup point, and in_app_calls is empty, while the platform detected the deviation at 11:30:14. So the agreed-deviation rows of POL-RD-24 are not open. But on a deviation of 1 km or less POL-RD-24 makes no refund conditional on notice (rows (c) and (e) both return no refund), so that finding moves no money.\n\nThe rider's contested sum of 2.00 SGD is not a figure this policy measures. POL-RD-24's excess distance fare would be deviation_km 0.60 × fare_breakdown.per_km_rate_sgd 0.72 = 0.43 SGD, and even on a refund row that is the most this trip could return. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-05002) shows payment_status CHARGED, total_charged 9.42 SGD and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the present state stands: under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION means the filing party's claim is not supported and no money moves. No clause of this policy produces a referral on a route deviation."
